{title: Lay Down His Life}
{subtitle: John 15:12–13}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
As the [Bb]Father has loved me
So I [Eb]have loved you
Remain in my [Gm7]love
Keep my com[Eb]mandments
[Bb]You will remain in my [Eb]love
[Cm]Just as I kept the [Gm]Father's
And [Eb]remained in his [Fsus4]love
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]This is my com[Bb]mandment
Love one an[Eb]other as I have [Gm]loved you
No one has [Fsus4]grea[Eb]ter love than this
[Gm]To lay down his [Eb][Fsus4]life for his [Bb]friends [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]You are my [Eb]friends
If you do what I command [Gm]you
I no longer [Eb]call you servants
A [Bb]servant does not know the [Eb]master's work
[Cm]But I have called you [Gm]friends
For everything [F]from the [Eb]Father
I have made known to [Fsus4]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This is my com[Bb]mandment
Love one anoth[Eb]er as I have loved [Gm]you
No one has grea[F]ter [Eb]love than this
To [Gm]lay down his life [F]for his [Bb]friends
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]You did not choose [Eb]me
But I chose [Bb]you
Ap[F/A]pointed you to go
And bear [Gm]fruit that will [Eb]last
So that what[Cm7]ever you ask
In my [Eb]name he will give [Fsus4][F]you
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This is my com[Bb]mandment
Love one anoth[Eb]er as I have loved you
[Gm]No one has greater [F]love [Eb]than this
To lay down [Gm]his life [Eb][F]for his [Bb]friends [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Lay down his life for his friends [Bb][Eb][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
